Name: MC_POLJETSHAPES_HARD
Summary: Particle-level jet-shape probes of polarized parton-shower spin correlations at 510 GeV
Status: UNVALIDATED
Reentrant: true
Authors:
  - Andreas Papaefstathiou <apapaefs@kennesaw.edu>
References:
  - Eur. Phys. J. C 81 (2021) 681
  - Phys. Rev. Lett. 126 (2021) 112003
RunInfo: Requires independent PP, PM, MP, and MM polarized pp samples.
NumEvents: 500000
NeedsCrossSection: yes
Beams: [p+, p+]
Energies: [510]
Options:
 - R=#
 - PTJ1MIN=#
 - PTJ2MIN=#
 - ETAMAX=#
Description: >
  Stable-visible-particle anti-kT R=0.5 dijets with pT1>5 GeV,
  pT2>4 GeV, and |eta|<1.5. Cambridge/Aachen reclustering defines
  signed primary-secondary and inter-jet splitting-plane angles without
  shower-history or flavour information. Each jet's intra-jet and hard-plane
  angles use its own 20-30 or 30-45 GeV half-open pT window. Event-level
  inter-jet angles, jet-3/4 spectra and radiation rates use the leading-jet
  window. Standard splittings have z1,z2>0.1 and kT>1 or 2 GeV. Hard-sharing
  declusterings require 0.25<z1<0.40 and z2>0.35 at matched kT thresholds
  of 1 or 2 GeV. All histograms retain compensated sampling event weights.
